comment.narrative:
1.1 Permits were obtained for the transboundary movement of PCB wastes planned for removal and destruction within the first stage.
An agreement was concluded with ROVAMI for the provision of services for the destruction of PCB equipment (second stage).
1.2 For the purpose of implementation at the Complex of management systems:
- of quality in accordance with the requirements of ISO 9001 “Quality management systems. Requirements ;
- of environment in accordance with the requirements of ISO 14001/STB ISO 14001 “Environmental Management Systems. Requirements and guidance for use”;
- of occupational health and safety in accordance with the requirements of ISO 45001 “Occupational health and safety management systems. Requirements and guidelines for use 
- the scope of certification is defined;
- the processes of management systems are identified and the points of their interaction are determined;
- the structure of documentation of management systems is defined;
- the subordination of employees and their responsibility are determined;
- employees were trained on how to work according to new procedures and standards, what records to fill out and with what frequency;
- a methodology for assessing the effectiveness of management systems was developed.
Further certification procedures are possible only after the facility at the Complex is put into operation. In order to conduct test incineration of the facility at the Complex, a method was developed and approved for determining the chemical composition of mixtures of obsolete pesticides, a sample out of 1000 containers with obsolete pesticides was made to analyze their chemical composition, and an analysis of the chemical composition of these wastes was carried out.
1.3 In order to organize the export of PCB equipment, permits were obtained for transboundary movement of waste (2 permits for the TREDI plant in France and the Veolia plant in Switzerland).
Holders of PCB equipment (stage 1) purchased packaging materials and packaged the waste.
As part of the second stage of destruction of PCB equipment:
- according to the results of the tender, the company ROVAMI was selected, with which a contract was concluded for the destruction of PCB equipment with a total weight of about 630 tons.
- ROVAMI prepared and submitted a package of documents for obtaining permission for the transboundary movement of PCB-containing equipment to the competent authorities of the countries of export, transit and import;
- the mechanism of waste consolidation was determined, the Complex was determined as the consolidation center;
between the Consolidation Center and 26 holders of PCB equipment, contracts were concluded for the provision of services for the preparation of waste for transboundary transportation.

2.1 620 tons of obsolete pesticides from the warehouses of Vitebsk and Grodno regions were removed and destroyed.
A service provider for the environmentally sound destruction of obsolete pesticides from warehouses in the Minsk region was selected.
2.2 1. A frontal survey of obsolete pesticides was carried out, including Dribin and Verkhnedvinsk burials of obsolete pesticides.
As part of the frontal survey, the following was performed:
- descriptions of research methods (methods) used to provide services for conducting a frontal survey of obsolete 
- pesticide burial sites were prepared;
- collection of information on disposals of obsolete pesticides, characterizing geomorphological, geological-hydrological and hydrogeochemical conditions;
- a reconnaissance survey of burial sites and adjacent territories was carried out;
- ground magnetic prospecting and aerial photography of burial sites were carried out;
- sampling of soils in the area of ??burial sites was carried out and measurements of their contamination with chemicals were carried out;
- analysis of local environmental monitoring data carried out within the framework of the National Environmental Monitoring System;
- reports with generalized materials on burials, which reflect the conclusions were prepared:
- on the content of chemicals, including pesticides, in groundwater in the area where burials are located;
- on the content of chemicals, including pesticides, in soils in areas where burials are located;
- on determination of approximate volumes of soils potentially contaminated with obsolete pesticides;
- an analysis of the impact of burials on the environment was carried out, including:
- calculation of the rate of spread of pesticides in groundwater and the formation of areas of environmental pollution in the areas of disposal of burials;
- assessment of the risk potential of the impact of burials on the environment and public health;
- assessment of the scale and degree of impact of burials on the environment.
- action plans for the elimination of burial sites were developed with an assessment of the timing of their implementation and cost, including a financial and economic justification.
The action plans were submitted to the land user for their further implementation.

3.1 A training session was held on the implementation of the requirements of the Technical Regulations of the Eurasian Economic Union On the safety of chemical products , in which 84 representatives of interested organizations improved their knowledge, including 74 women and 10 men.
3.2 Folders, calendars with information on POPs for representatives of interested organizations were published and distributed. A seminar on regulation of waste management, including those containing POPs, was held, in which representatives of interested organizations, including women and men, improved their knowledge.
3.3 The Unified POPs database has been modernized, including the automation of processing of information resources of state statistics 1-Waste of the Ministry of Natural Resources. The national program for monitoring chemicals in environmental objects has been expanded.
3.4 In the course of modernization of the Unified POPs database, the functionality of the Unified POPs database expanded in terms of the possibility of entering data on new POPs.
3.5 A computer game for devices on Android and iOS systems on POPs issues was developed to raise public awareness about POPs issues.

4.1 Two meetings of the Project Board held.
4.2 An annual spot check and an audit of the Ministry of Natural Resources and Environmental Protection of the Republic of Belarus were conducted by a third-party service provider in accordance with the Agreed Approach of the UN Development Group to the money transfer system carried out.
4.3 Translation services are provided by the State Institution “Republican Center for Analytical Control in the Field of Environmental Protection” properly and on time.
4.4 Translation services are provided by the State Institution “Republican Center for Analytical Control in the Field of Environmental Protection” properly and on time.

1.1 Preparations for the removal of at least 430 tons of PCB equipment from the Republic of Belarus for disposal started. An open tender for the provision of services for the environmentally sound disposal of about 630 tons of PCB equipment organized. An assessment of the possible cross-contamination of electrical equipment that does not contain PCBs (at least 500 units) conducted. The methodology for assessing the possible cross-contamination of electrical equipment that does not contain PCBs sent to at least 3 service companies for further implementation as a standard practice.
1.2 Monitoring of the implementation of the project for the creation of facilities for the destruction of waste on the basis of the Complex in the Chechersk region was conducted.
Interaction with the UNIDO / GEF international technical assistance project “Regional Demonstration Project for Coordinated Management of ODS and POPs Disposal in Ukraine, Belarus, Kazakhstan and Armenia” on the preparation of terms of reference for the provision of support services in the certification of this installation.
A draft terms of reference for an international expert has been prepared to provide support in the certification of facilities for the destruction of waste generated on the basis of the Complex.
1.3 The preparation of PCB equipment in the amount of about 430 tons has begun for export from the Republic of Belarus for environmentally sound disposal - the first stage. An open tender was organized for the provision of services for the environmentally sound disposal of existing stocks of PCB equipment (about 630 tons) - the second stage.

2.1 The preparation of 920 tons of obsolete pesticides from the warehouses of the Vitebsk and Grodno regions was carried. 97.042 tons of obsolete pesticides were exported outside the Republic of Belarus and environmentally sound destroyed .
Warehouses of organizations are completely cleared of obsolete pesticides:
OJSC Dubrovensky Raiagroservice ;
JSC Lepelagroservice;
State Enterprise Ustye NAS of Belarus ;
JSC Vitebsk Broiler Poultry Factory ;
JSC Belenevo ;
Unitary Enterprise Mnyuto ;
SE Lomashi-Agro ;
JSC Sharkovshchinsky agrotechservice ;
OJSC Glubokoye Agroservice ;
OJSC Braslavsky rayagroservice ;
Vitebsk customs.
The terms of reference for the provision of services for the environmentally sound destruction of about 500 tons of obsolete pesticides stored in the warehouses of the Minsk region have been prepared. An open tender was organized for the provision of services for the environmentally sound destruction of about 500 tons of obsolete pesticides stored in the warehouses of the Minsk region.
2.2 . As part of the preparation of action plans for the elimination of Petrikov, Gorodok and Postavy burials of obsolete pesticides, the following actions were carried out:
- collection of information on burials of obsolete pesticides, characterizing geomorphological, geological-hydrological and hydrogeochemical conditions;
- reconnaissance surveys of the burial sites and the surrounding area were carried out;
- ground magnetic survey and aerial photography of burial sites were carried out;
- sampling of soils in the area of ??disposal of burials was carried out and measurements of their contamination with -chemical substances were carried out;
- analysis of data from local environmental monitoring was carried out within the framework of the National Environmental Monitoring System;
- reports with summarized information on the disposal were prepared, which reflect the conclusions:
- on the content of chemicals, including pesticides, in groundwater in the area of ??the disposal site;
- on the content of chemicals, including pesticides, in the soils in the area of ??the disposal site;
- on the determination of indicative volumes of potentially contaminated soil with obsolete pesticides;
- an analysis of the impact of disposal on the environment was carried out, including:
- calculation of the rate of spread of pesticides in groundwater and the formation of an area of ??environmental pollution in the area of ??the disposal site;
- assessment of the potential risks of the impact of disposal on the environment and public health;
- assessment of the scale and degree of the impact of disposal on the environment;
- an action plan for the elimination of the burial was developed with an assessment of the timing of their implementation and cost, including a financial and economic justification.
The action plans were transferred to the user of natural resources for their further implementation.
Proposals have been prepared for a project application to the GEF for the elimination of Petrikov, Gorodok and Postavy burials of obsolete pesticides.

3.1 Activity is planned for 2022.
3.2 During the international specialized ecological exhibition-forum Ecology Expo - 2021 and the XVI Republican Ecological Forum Involvement of Civil Society in Environmental Decision Making , more than 1000 visitors were shown the dynamics of utilization of obsolete pesticides in the Republic of Belarus until 2030.
A round table Improving the waste management system was held, during which more than 80 representatives of local authorities, environmental organizations and the population, especially women, increased their knowledge in the field of POPs.
Information materials were published on raising the awareness of the population, especially women, about POPs.
Through the Committees of Natural Resources and Environmental Protection of the Republic of Belarus, information materials were brought to the attention of the population.
POPs information posters were published. The posters were handed over to the Complex for placement on information stands.
3.3 The terms of reference for the provision of services for the modernization of the Unified POPs database, including the automation of the processing of information resources of the state statistical reporting 1-Waste of the Ministry of Natural Resources, has been prepared.
A tender was held to select a contractor for the provision of the above services for the modernization of the Unified database on POPs, including the automation of the processing of information resources of the state statistical reporting 1-Waste of the Ministry of Natural Resources.
3.4 A test version of the modernized Unified Database on POPs has been developed, including a complex for the automation of the reception and processing of the 1-waste state statistical reporting (Ministry of Natural Resources).
3.5 Videos on POPs issues were created, including a 5-minute version and a 30-second (shortened) version for demonstration on TV. The thematic site and forum are functioning, interested persons have the opportunity to discuss problems related to POPs.

4.1 A mid-term evaluation of the project has been completed. A mid-term evaluation report has been prepared.
4.2 3 meetings of the Project Board held.
4.3 Recommendations based on the results of the audit of the financial activities of the Ministry of Natural Resources, aimed at the implementation of the project, were taken into account in the subsequent implementation of the project.
4.4 Translation services are provided by the State Institution “Republican Center for Analytical Control in the Field of Environmental Protection” properly and on time.
4.5 33 procurement procedures were carried out, as a result of which 34 (including 9 contracts for the environmentally sound disposal of PCB equipment) contracts for the provision of services and the supply of goods were concluded. Procurement specialist services are provided as appropriate.
